<!--Post: 122--><!--Time: 1085787718-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST122"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 4:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t know how relevant this is,if at all, however, I found the case of Cherie Fox interesting.I suppose we have to wonder if BTK was still killing all these years. <BR>Cherie Fox was murdered on the 12th of september 1996. Perhaps it&#39;s just the name and timing. <BR>Cherie &#40;16 years old&#41; was only living in Wichita for a month.Moved there from Arizona with her father. On sept 12th Cherie was getting ready for work at 7:30 am as her father was leaving the house. He returned at 11am to find here lying on the bed. She had been shot. The address is listed as 2150 South Meridian in Wichita. Coincidentally or not, I believe the 12th was a thursday. No sign of forced entry. Quote:-&#34; Police believe she knew her murderer&#34;. I assume this may have been because of the above fact!. <BR>One wonders how many peole she could have actually know, being there only a month. She worked at an area restuarant! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 122-->
<!--Post: 267--><!--Time: 1086975267-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST267"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 10:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->She had been shot. I think BTK only used his gun if he had to. I don&#39;t think he would have to with a 16 yr old girl. It seems to me he only uses a gun to get people to do what he wants them to. Then he does what he does. In dire situations like with Katherine Bright he goes stab happy, in extremely dire situations as with Kevin Bright then he actually uses the gun. I really don&#39;t see any reason for him to shoot a 16 yo girl. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 267-->
<!--Post: 274--><!--Time: 1087144761-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Colette<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Colette<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An older BTK may have had more of a physical challenge with a fit 16 year old girl.. therefore used a gun ala Kevin Bright.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 274-->
<!--Post: 280--><!--Time: 1087159802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 1:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Age/size/gender does not necessarily have anything to do with someone&#39;s ability to fight back.  When I was 16yo, I could pin down almost every guy in the firehouse where I volunteered &#40;there was one who could kick my butt, though&#41;.  Additionally, once one of my friends from the firehouse &#40;which is in a bad part of town&#41; snuck up behind me as I was getting into my car late one night and grabbed me.  Adrenaline kicked in and he was on the ground before I had time to see who it was or even think about what I was doing.  Even though I was very fit at the time, and I&#39;m fairly tall, I&#39;ve seen a 5&#39;0&#34; petite firefighter fight very well when wrestling with the guys.  She knew how to use leverage to her advantage and I believe she was trained in one of the martial arts. <BR> <BR>My long-winded point is, I don&#39;t think the use of the gun had anything to do with the genders of the victims.  I think he likely brought it to most/all of his crimes to intimidate and only used it when his victims didn&#39;t cooporate.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 280-->
<!--Post: 282--><!--Time: 1087165672-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 3:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s a good point Muskogee. But for whatever reason, I wouldn&#39;t rule out BTK here because a gun was used. She was only living in Wichita for a month. While not impossible, it&#39;s hardly long enough to get to know people, not to mind make an enemy of someone &#40;she knows&#41; who was willing to kill her. <BR>It&#39;s also hard to believe that some other person, who decided to kill her, for whatever reason,would strike that early in the morning.That person must have watched the house and waited until her father left.It is also curious in those circumstances that she ended up in the bedroom. <BR>She could have met her killer at her workplace. <BR>Just thoughts!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 282-->
<!--Post: 283--><!--Time: 1087165774-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST283"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Colette<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Colette<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, June 13, 2004 - 3:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Right... &#34;fighting back&#34; IS not cooporating.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 283-->
<!--Post: 289--><!--Time: 1087234873-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 14, 2004 - 10:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sean, I agree...I wouldn&#39;t rule him out either.  I think you make a good point about her living there such a short time &#40;though I&#39;m sure she could have encountered some strange people while working in the restraunt&#41;.   <BR> <BR>Unfortunately, we don&#39;t know on what evidence the police based their statement that they believe she knew her murderer.  If it&#39;s based soley on the fact that there was no sign of forced entry, I&#39;d say that&#39;s pretty weak.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 289-->
<!--Post: 297--><!--Time: 1087301243-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST297"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Colette<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Colette<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 15, 2004 - 5:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Right..BTK could have used a fake ID and a ruse to get her to open the door.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 297-->
<!--Post: 9468--><!--Time: 1109536274-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9468"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was there any strangulation?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9468-->
